  "lesson": {
    "prerequisite_note": "You can edit text and distinguish saved work from running state. This separate example introduces unit dependencies and future-session enablement.",
    "concepts": [
      {
        "title": "Saved text, manager definitions and running programs",
        "text": "Saving changes the editor file. Manager reload reads unit definitions; it does not restart a program. Application configuration is consumed when that fictional program initializes."
      },
      {
        "title": "Bring it in, then put it in order",
        "text": "Requires asks for another unit to start. After says to wait for its start job. A successful prepare oneshot supplies data; starting a simple service still needs its separate simulated initialization event."
      },
      {
        "title": "Now and next session are separate",
        "text": "Start affects current runtime. Enable adds a future target link; selecting the default chooses which target a fresh-session test starts. None of these actions changes your real machine."
      }
    ],
